The _WAK method should be run as the very last thing in 
AcpiLeaveSleepState(), after GPEs are enabled, BM enabled, etc.  The 
reason is that _WAK often contains Notifys which may cause the system to 
generate GPEs.  This fits with the spec.  Also, it would be helpful to 
print the return status (under the ACPI_DEBUG) option so that we can 
track down more info why a suspend failed if it did.

-Nate


